ers-kristinarash-DEV-<X>` on the Mac and `C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV-<X>` on Windows (Windows is active again as of 2026-09-10). Tier A written on one machine is not auto-injected on the other; memsearch still finds it. Prefer writing durable project facts to the repo's `docs/` so both machines see them.\n\n## Tier B — global working memory\n`~/.claude/global-memory/`, loaded every session regardless of cwd:\n- `USER.md` — durable user profile. **1,375 character cap.**\n- `MEMORY.md` — active threads, environment notes, pending decisions. **2,500 character cap.**\n- `transcripts/YYYY-MM-DD.md` — auto-captured turn summaries (Stop hook).\n\nCheck `wc -c` before writing. If over cap, consolidate existing entries before adding.\n\n## Daily compiled logs (separate system, read-only)\n`~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/daily/{YYYY-MM-DD}.md`, produced by `claude-memory-compiler` via its own hooks. **Never write to them manually. Never read them eagerly** — treat the injected snapshot as the source of truth.\n\n## Session startup (silent — output nothing)\n\n> Kept as a manual instruction on purpose. Claude Code does this with the\n> `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook, so `CLAUDE.md` no longer\n> states it. Codex has no equivalent hook, so the steps stay spelled out here.\n> Do not \"align\" the two files by deleting this section.\nRead in this order: `global-memory/USER.md`, then `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, then `global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. If `.errors.log` is non-empty, surface its contents once on the first response, then continue. It should normally be empty; entries indicate hook failures.\n\nThese are a **frozen snapshot** — loaded once. Mid-session writes persist to disk but take effect next session. This preserves the prefix cache. Never load more than this proactively.\n\n## Writing — the steps\nOn \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"update memory\", \"save this\", \"forget about\":\n1. Decide tier — \"will this be true and useful in 3 months, across projects?\" Yes → Tier A. No / only matters now → Tier B.\n2. Read the target file in full.\n3. Dedup check (substring scan).\n4. Cap check (`wc -c`) for Tier B.\n5. If over cap, consolidate before adding.\n6. Write.\n7. Confirm in one line: `Saved — will be active from next session.`\n\nFor **remove**: confirm with the user before deleting.\n\n## Retrieval — the tiered ladder\nClimb in order; stop as soon as the question is answered. Do not run memsearch when the answer is already in the injected snapshot.\n\n1. **Tier 0** — scan what is already in context (USER.md, MEMORY.md, today's compiled log). Zero cost.\n2. **L1** — `memsearch search \"query\" --top-k 5`. Hybrid vector + keyword across all indexed paths.\n3. **L2** — `memsearch expand <chunk_hash>`. Full markdown section around a hit.\n4. **L3** — `memsearch transcript <session_id>`. Raw dialogue. Last resort.\n5. **Fallback** — \"I don't have a record of that.\"\n\n== USER.md\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash — Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds athlete performance data pipelines (Football GPS, force plate). Family: wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo as of 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-forward player-coach near Iowa, ~$90K+ floor, ~mid-2027. Deeper context: `~/DEV/ContextVault` — read before career/personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python + R. **macOS since 2026-08-05**; Windows 11 box still ACTIVE (synced 9/9). Tool paths: see CLAUDE.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB; no cloud/servers/schedulers without Baylor IT approval. OneDrive project folders — beware DuckDB locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Wants to be challenged, not affirmed — push on vague or rehearsed reasoning (\"sharpened, not soothed\").\n- Defers technical micro-decisions when convention exists — decide, state it, move on.\n- Builds incrementally. Nothing that breaks mid-season.\n- Authors own direction when leadership doesn't; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo org.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n== global MEMORY.md\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: `DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash/`, pushed 9/9. NEXT: real-phone check; host or keep local. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes.\n- **Baseball profiles (9/2)**: `DEV/Baseball_PerformanceProfiles`, Excel-only coach. 3 .xlsx mock-data prototypes. NEXT: coach picks one + real tests.\n- **RTP CLA course (9/10)**: ingest + PDF rebuild DONE. NEXT: import .ris → Zotero; lesson 0002. →Tier A rtp-cla-course.\n- **ATH Tech framework (8/14)**: shipped. NEXT: Micah mtg (need ITS intake path); inventory refresh due 9/29. →Tier A ath-tech-framework, tech-inventory-refresh.\n- **Kinexon volleyball (8/1)**: API email→CSM, awaiting docs. Plan: sync→SQLite→dashboards; CSV interim.\n- **Status report (9/7)**: #2 drafted, UNSENT — `SecondBrain/Inbox/status-reports/2026-09-07-email.txt`. NEXT: read-check, send, rename `-email-sent.txt`, flip `sent: true`. #3 = 9/21. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline.\n- **Acro & Tumbling (9/8)**: owe an Excel \"pass builder\" — routines → cumulative impact load. 5-athlete pilot. Awaiting skill inventory + assignments.\n- **Open PRs (9/7)**: AgentAssist #1 (draft), CFB_Analytics_Lab #1. Deferred: FA26 camp regex.\n- **OKR/JD 2026 (7/17)**: Blake LEFT, AJ owns FB. →vault `Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026/`.\n- Parked in Tier A: Fireflies key rotation; child dental.\n\n- **Skill audit (9/12)**: DONE. 160→61 global skills, 19.2k→6.4k tok/session. Plugins beat local copies. →Tier A skill-bloat-and-promotion\n\n## Environment Notes\n- **Portfolio dashboard** LIVE; `/project` re-renders+republishes. →Tier A command-centre, portfolio-registry-write-provenance.\n- **Terminal (9/4)**: tmux = default VS Code shell; `cc`/`cx` aliases. →vault `Knowledge/tooling/tmux-cheat-sheet.md`.\n- Hooks exist in TWO copies (`.claude/hooks/`, `.codex/hooks/`) — patch both. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo (`erash11/DEV`), 8 router `.md` only; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. `_ARCHIVE/` = parked. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Schedules/gws limits →automation-cadence. CFB capture (Mon, 8/24–1/23) →cfb-forecast-capture.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- **DUE (was 8/31)**: OKR Q1 gate: AI integration (buy-in) + data governance (Anthony's proposal).\n- **Kitman vs MyLink**: MyLink intros (~half Kitman's cost) + buy Kitman API access. Undecided; blocks priority 3.\n\n== DEV AGENTS.md\n# AGENTS.md — ~/DEV workspace root\n\nThis repo tracks ONLY the workspace router files. It holds no project code.\nEach project folder under `~/DEV` is its own git repo with its own remote.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## What lives here\n`CLAUDE.md` is the workspace map. Read it first, then the one area index you need:\n`FOOTBALL.md`, `PERFORMANCE.md`, `RESEARCH.md`, `PLATFORM.md`, `PROGRAM.md`,\n`PERSONAL.md`, `COMMANDS.md`.\n\nNote: `CLAUDE.md` here is NOT the usual one-line `@AGENTS.md` pointer. It is the\nreal workspace map and Claude Code loads it automatically. Leave it that way.\n\n## Do not\n- Do not `git add` a project folder. They are separate repos on purpose.\n- Do not remove the `/*` rule in `.gitignore`. It is what keeps this repo thin.\n== outputStyle/skillOverrides/env\noutputStyle ELI5\nskillOverrides {\"session-handoff\": \"user-invocable-only\", \"ApertureOscillation\": \"off\", \"Aphorisms\": \"off\", \"Apify\": \"off\", \"Art\": \"off\", \"AudioEditor\": \"off\", \"BeCreative\": \"off\", \"BiasCheck\": \"off\", \"BitterPillEngineering\": \"off\", \"BrightData\": \"off\", \"ContextSearch\": \"off\", \"Council\": \"off\", \"CreateCLI\": \"off\", \"Daemon\": \"off\", \"Delegation\": \"off\", \"Evals\": \"off\", \"ExtractWisdom\": \"off\", \"Fabric\": \"off\", \"FirstPrinciples\": \"off\", \"Hardening\": \"off\", \"Ideate\": \"off\", \"Interceptor\": \"off\", \"IterativeDepth\": \"off\", \"LocalIntelligence\": \"off\", \"Loop\": \"off\", \"Migrate\": \"off\", \"Optimize\": \"off\", \"PrivateInvest\nenv keys ['CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_TERMINAL_TITLE']\nELI5.md\n     680 output-styles/ELI5.md\n== skills CLAUDE.md\n    1370 skills/CLAUDE.md\n    1370 total\ntotal 80\ndrwx------@  4 kristinarash  staff    128 Aug 15 14:17 _shared\ndrwx------@ 71 kristinarash  staff   2272 Sep 12 18:05 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  71 kristinarash  staff   2272 Sep 13 01:25 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 kristinarash  staff    128 Aug 15 17:43 .claude\n== is skills a symlink\ntotal 24\nlrwxr-xr-x@   1 kristinarash  staff    42 Sep 12 18:07 _shared -> /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/_shared\ndrwxr-xr-x  217 kristinarash  staff  6944 Sep 12 18:07 .","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"65cf0cb9-9d07-4025-8b20-27e1210a5593","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
