{"parentUuid":"0bc37faa-cf57-4bf8-8938-4374623cf85c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab4fe4e9201583637","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezyCwh3PRU1rV4iDRGhu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0122dzLv5hCFFrkSMJ2oK9dE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude; echo \"== skill-bloat memo\"; cat projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md | head -40; echo \"== hook-two-copies memo\"; cat projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_hook-two-copies-trap.md | head -30; echo \"== memory-write Windows\"; grep -n \"retired\\|Windows\" skills/memory-write/SKILL.md | cut -c1-200","description":"Read recorded decisions and memory-write Windows lines"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5884,"cache_read_input_tokens":74645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5884,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CezyCvnxzh4mCa4Q7WCko","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"update-config","type":"assistant","uuid":"681340cf-ccbe-4b70-a71f-17135eea0476","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:34:18.838Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"681340cf-ccbe-4b70-a71f-17135eea0476","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4ebb38d0-21a0-49af-a2e5-2733be1f3595","agentId":"ab4fe4e9201583637","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0122dzLv5hCFFrkSMJ2oK9dE","type":"tool_result","content":"== skill-bloat memo\n---\nname: skill-bloat-and-promotion\ndescription: \"Measured skill bloat in this setup, the project-until-promoted rule that fixes it, and the command that re-measures usage from .jsonl session logs\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d\n  modified: 2026-09-12T22:59:50.121Z\n---\n\nMeasured 2026-09-12 from a gap analysis of a Nate Herk / **Mark Kashef** video\n(\"How to Actually Choose the Right AI Agent\", 2026-09-11). Full note:\n`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`.\nSame shape as the earlier audit in [[brain-audit-loop]] — that one scored the\n**vault**, this one scores the **skill layer**.\n\n## The measurement\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Global skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | 160 (→ **117** after the Tier 1 archive, 2026-09-12) |\n| Plugin skills exposed per session | ~37 (6 enabled, 18 disabled) |\n| SKILL.md files in plugin cache | 606 — disabled plugins + old versions, NOT the load |\n| Project-level skills anywhere in `~/DEV` | **0** |\n| `.jsonl` sessions scanned | 414 |\n| Distinct real skills **ever** invoked | **58** |\n| Used 3+ times | 30 |\n| Used exactly once | 19 |\n\nEverything is global. That is the anti-pattern, not the achievement.\n\n## The rule that fixes it — promotion\n\n**Everything stays project-level until it earns global.** A skill lives in\n`<project>/.claude/skills/` until it proves itself across 2+ projects, then it\ngets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/`. Keeps the global load small and the blast\nradius tight — so when something underperforms you can tell a *model* problem\nfrom a *harness* problem from an *organisation* problem.\n\n## The audit question\n== hook-two-copies memo\n---\nname: hook-two-copies-trap\ndescription: \"A Claude Code hook patch works, then silently reverts — hooks live in two directories and both must be patched\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 9422b1a6-8624-4c86-a4f6-3c4b1a4c9fc8\n  modified: 2026-09-09T15:26:04.471Z\n---\n\nThe **entire hook directory is mirrored** across two harnesses — not one stray file.\nVerified 2026-09-09: ~55 near-identical entries in each of\n\n- `~/.claude/hooks/` — Claude Code\n- `~/.codex/hooks/` — Codex\n\n**Patch both, always.** Editing one leaves the other on the old code. Whichever\nharness runs next re-triggers the bug, which reads as \"the fix reverted\".\n\nThe two are not exact mirrors, so do not assume drift means a failed patch:\n`.claude/hooks/` additionally holds `herdr-agent-state.sh` and an older\n`memsearch-sync.js.bak-20260814`. Those are legitimate, not drift.\n\nWorked example — `transcript-capture.js` (Stop hook):\nCodex invokes it with a null `transcript_path`, which the script did not handle.\nPatched 2026-09-07 to exit quietly on null instead of erroring.\n**Tell that a copy drifted:** `missing transcript_path` lines reappear in\n`~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. When they do, diff the two\ncopies before debugging the script itself.\n\n== memory-write Windows\n80:2. **L1** — `memsearch search \"query\" --top-k 5`. Hybrid vector + keyword across all indexed paths: Tier A files (including the retired Windows slugs), daily logs, transcripts.\n101:- **Never write to a `C--Users-eric-rash*` slug.** Those are pre-migration Windows keys from the box retired 2026-08-14. They are still indexed by memsearch, so old facts stay recallable, but noth","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"172c5f82-baa2-4d58-b013-c0117a8900fc","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:34:20.427Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"== skill-bloat memo\n---\nname: skill-bloat-and-promotion\ndescription: \"Measured skill bloat in this setup, the project-until-promoted rule that fixes it, and the command that re-measures usage from .jsonl session logs\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d\n  modified: 2026-09-12T22:59:50.121Z\n---\n\nMeasured 2026-09-12 from a gap analysis of a Nate Herk / **Mark Kashef** video\n(\"How to Actually Choose the Right AI Agent\", 2026-09-11). Full note:\n`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`.\nSame shape as the earlier audit in [[brain-audit-loop]] — that one scored the\n**vault**, this one scores the **skill layer**.\n\n## The measurement\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Global skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | 160 (→ **117** after the Tier 1 archive, 2026-09-12) |\n| Plugin skills exposed per session | ~37 (6 enabled, 18 disabled) |\n| SKILL.md files in plugin cache | 606 — disabled plugins + old versions, NOT the load |\n| Project-level skills anywhere in `~/DEV` | **0** |\n| `.jsonl` sessions scanned | 414 |\n| Distinct real skills **ever** invoked | **58** |\n| Used 3+ times | 30 |\n| Used exactly once | 19 |\n\nEverything is global. That is the anti-pattern, not the achievement.\n\n## The rule that fixes it — promotion\n\n**Everything stays project-level until it earns global.** A skill lives in\n`<project>/.claude/skills/` until it proves itself across 2+ projects, then it\ngets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/`. Keeps the global load small and the blast\nradius tight — so when something underperforms you can tell a *model* problem\nfrom a *harness* problem from an *organisation* problem.\n\n## The audit question\n== hook-two-copies memo\n---\nname: hook-two-copies-trap\ndescription: \"A Claude Code hook patch works, then silently reverts — hooks live in two directories and both must be patched\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 9422b1a6-8624-4c86-a4f6-3c4b1a4c9fc8\n  modified: 2026-09-09T15:26:04.471Z\n---\n\nThe **entire hook directory is mirrored** across two harnesses — not one stray file.\nVerified 2026-09-09: ~55 near-identical entries in each of\n\n- `~/.claude/hooks/` — Claude Code\n- `~/.codex/hooks/` — Codex\n\n**Patch both, always.** Editing one leaves the other on the old code. Whichever\nharness runs next re-triggers the bug, which reads as \"the fix reverted\".\n\nThe two are not exact mirrors, so do not assume drift means a failed patch:\n`.claude/hooks/` additionally holds `herdr-agent-state.sh` and an older\n`memsearch-sync.js.bak-20260814`. Those are legitimate, not drift.\n\nWorked example — `transcript-capture.js` (Stop hook):\nCodex invokes it with a null `transcript_path`, which the script did not handle.\nPatched 2026-09-07 to exit quietly on null instead of erroring.\n**Tell that a copy drifted:** `missing transcript_path` lines reappear in\n`~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. When they do, diff the two\ncopies before debugging the script itself.\n\n== memory-write Windows\n80:2. **L1** — `memsearch search \"query\" --top-k 5`. Hybrid vector + keyword across all indexed paths: Tier A files (including the retired Windows slugs), daily logs, transcripts.\n101:- **Never write to a `C--Users-eric-rash*` slug.** Those are pre-migration Windows keys from the box retired 2026-08-14. They are still indexed by memsearch, so old facts stay recallable, but noth","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"681340cf-ccbe-4b70-a71f-17135eea0476","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
