{"parentUuid":"29284e34-3ecd-4b8c-bf6a-0e184ac4aa96","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab4fe4e9201583637","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezyQVXmfEsrkcuDpqCt2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8198,"cache_read_input_tokens":80529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8198,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CezyQUdgrmbzLF6VwRJ5M","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"update-config","type":"assistant","uuid":"acb1ebbc-245f-4200-94b4-7372e16af509","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:34:50.003Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"acb1ebbc-245f-4200-94b4-7372e16af509","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab4fe4e9201583637","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezyQVXmfEsrkcuDpqCt2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Context posture audit (doctor-plus, part 2), 2026-09-13, read-only\n\nOverall: all six shifts are AMBER, except shift 6, which is GREEN. The biggest problem is under shift 4: the `memory-write` skill contradicts every other file about whether the Windows laptop is in use, and that skill is the one set to win.\n\n## 1. The six shifts\n\n**Shift 1, judgement over rules: AMBER**\n- The always-loaded files are lean. `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` has 4 absolutes, `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md` has 1, and all of them are safety or design rules. None should be flagged.\n- Worst offender: `~/.claude/skills/CLAUDE.md` (1,370 bytes). The rule is \"use CreateSkill\", but about 3x that much text enforces it (\"MANDATORY\", \"STOP\", \"is NOT compliance\").\n- That file also cites `feedback_invoke_blogging_skill_never_handroll.md`. I searched `~/.claude`, `~/DEV` and `~/SecondBrain` and the file is not there.\n- `design-taste-frontend` has 23 absolute rules about taste. Its `-v1` copy has 31. The `-v1` copy is on disk but not in the session skill list, so it is probably shadowed.\n- Fix: cut the enforcement block to one sentence and remove the broken citation.\n\n**Shift 2, interfaces over examples: AMBER**\n- The skill scaffold makes examples mandatory. `CreateSkill/Workflows/CreateSkill.md:289` requires \"`## Examples` section with 2-3 concrete usage patterns\", and `ValidateSkill.md:112` checks for it. So every new skill is built from examples.\n- The `pp-*` skills have many code blocks (29, 27, 23), but they are command references and recipes, not worked examples. Not flagged.\n- Fix: make Examples optional in the scaffold and validator. Require clear names and inputs instead.\n\n**Shift 3, progressive disclosure: AMBER**\n- Every session loads about:\n  - `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` 3.4k + `machine.md` 1.3k + `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md` 2.7k\n  - `USER.md` 1.3k + `MEMORY.md` 2.5k\n  - project `MEMORY.md` 6.6k\n  - descriptions of the 61 local skills: 27.7k chars, about 6.9k tokens\n  - about 40 plugin skills (not measured)\n  - up to 6k of daily log\n- Good design already in place: the KeystoneOS snapshot is point-only, and the 71k knowledge index is a pointer.\n- Offenders:\n  - Skill descriptions that are long lists of trigger phrases: `scroll-craft` 1,174 chars, `impeccable` 895, `ISA` 850, `CreateSkill` 787.\n  - The project memory index breaks its own \"never put memory content here\" header. Some lines carry facts, for example \"morning-cadence dies on a `C:\\`…\" and \"reminder sent 9/8\".\n  - Global `MEMORY.md` is 2,489 of its 2,500-char cap.\n  - Project CLAUDE.md files load in full: FaceComps 27.1k, PlayCalls 21.6k, Ath_Medicine 21.2k.\n- Fix: cut descriptions to under about 400 chars, and move facts out of index lines into the memory files they point to.\n\n**Shift 4, one home per rule: AMBER (the most serious finding)**\n- **Contradiction.** `skills/memory-write/SKILL.md:101` says the Windows box was \"retired 2026-08-14\" and \"Never write to a `C--Users-eric-rash*` slug\".\n  - `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md:31`, `AGENTS.md:30` and `USER.md:8` all say Windows is active again (9/9, 9/10).\n  - `AGENTS.md` says memory-write \"wins\" when they disagree, so the stale rule wins.\n- The `dcg` guard is registered twice under PreToolUse in `settings.json`: once by absolute path, once as a guarded exec. It runs twice on every Bash call.\n- The two hook copies differ:\n  - `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` is 3,399 bytes in `~/.claude/hooks` and 856 bytes in `~/.codex/hooks`. It may be a deliberate Codex stub, but the hook-two-copies memo does not list it as an allowed difference.\n  - `transcript-capture.js` differs in comments only.\n- Fix: update memory-write lines 80 and 101 to match the \"both machines active\" state, and remove one `dcg` entry.\n\n**Shift 5, auto-memory over guidance-file memory: AMBER globally, RED in projects**\n- Global:\n  - `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` says \"Both machines are active as of 2026-09-10\".\n  - `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md` says \"Counts last checked 2026-09-05\".\n- Projects:\n  - `Ath_Medicine/CLAUDE.md` has 19 dates. It has a \"## Status\" section (\"All 24 columns … complete as of 2026-06-13\") plus 8 analysis-result sections dated 06-13/06-14, about 200 lines.\n  - `Football/FaceComps/CLAUDE.md:80` has \"Fall Camp 2026 mode — BUILT & DEPLOYED (2026-05-24)\" and coaching staff lists.\n  - Also `PlayerProfiles_FB` (9 dates) and `cmj-traffic-light` (7 dates).\n- 113 of 115 top-level repos already have `docs/STATUS.md`.\n- Fix: move status and findings sections into `docs/STATUS.md` or a findings doc, and keep CLAUDE.md for how to work in the project.\n\n**Shift 6, rich references over simple specs: GREEN**\n- Active builds use real references:\n  - `Baseball_PerformanceProfiles` has 3 `.xlsx` prototypes plus `gen_prototypes.py`.\n  - `CFB_Analytics_Lab` has 15 test files.\n  - `Kinexon_Volleyball` has `tests/`.\n  - FaceComps has a design spec, a plan, and working code.\n- `AgentAssist` has 27 `.md` files and no tests, but its product is markdown agent definitions, so that is expected.\n- The Acro \"pass builder\" exists only as a line in `MEMORY.md`, with no project folder yet.\n- Fix: when Acro starts, make a mock `.xlsx` first, as was done for Baseball.\n\n## 2. Checked\n- Read the doctor-plus skill.\n- Measured sizes of: global CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, machine.md, TOOLPATHS.md, `global-memory/{USER,MEMORY}.md`, the `~/DEV` router `.md` files, and the project memory index.\n- Parsed `settings.json` for hooks, skill overrides and output style. Read the ELI5 style and `skills/CLAUDE.md`.\n- Read the injection logic in `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` and the compiler's `session-start.py`, and sized the KeystoneOS snapshot and knowledge index.\n- Parsed the frontmatter of all 61 `~/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` for description length, code-block count and absolute-rule count.\n- Checked `CreateSkill` Workflows for the Examples requirement.\n- Listed every project CLAUDE.md to depth 4 by size and date count, and pulled the cited lines from Ath_Medicine and FaceComps.\n- Compared the two hook directories with `cmp` and diffed the ones that differ.\n- Compared caps and Windows wording between memory-write and AGENTS.md. Caps match; the Windows status does not.\n- Read the `skill-bloat-and-promotion` and `hook-two-copies-trap` memory files.\n- Checked tests, spreadsheets and specs in 6 active builds, and counted STATUS.md files.\n- Every command was read-only. Two used `> /dev/null`, and one glob gave a harmless \"no matches\" error. No file was touched.\n\n## 3. Not checked\n- **`/doctor` and `claude doctor`:** interactive, and skipped as instructed. Run `/doctor` in your own session for that half.\n- **Plugin skill description size:** 564 plugin SKILL.md files are cached, but most are disabled plugins or old versions. The per-session count of about 40 comes from the session skill list, not a measurement.\n- **`~/.agents/skills`** (213 entries vs 61): outside scope. I spot-checked 4 and they were identical.\n- **Not scanned:** project CLAUDE.md files deeper than depth 4, `_ARCHIVE`, and nested per-directory CLAUDE.md files other than `skills/`.\n- **Not scanned:** the content of the 50 project memory files, beyond the index and the two memos.\n- **DexaProject:** excluded, as required.\n- **Fixes:** none applied, as the skill requires approval first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8198,"cache_read_input_tokens":80529,"output_tokens":3798,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":702},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8198},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":3798,"cache_read_input_tokens":80529,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8198,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CezyQUdgrmbzLF6VwRJ5M","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"update-config","type":"assistant","uuid":"37cdeb60-ba4f-4e0d-9f3c-aff861d6f19c","timestamp":"2026-09-13T06:35:15.736Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9823c1f0-89f5-4638-9223-c6892607ac2b","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
